Thu Aug 20 08:53:50 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Convert the Python binding to the shared
  %treesitter_python_install loader (flavor subpackages). The
  compiled _binding extension is not built: the macro installs
  upstream's pure-Python package files and generates a _binding.py
  that loads the grammar library this package ships, so the parser
  is not compiled a second time and no python devel/pip/wheel
  BuildRequires are needed.
- The python subpackage pins the grammar package exactly.
- Suggests python-tree-sitter >= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package.
- Run a functional %check parsing Groovy source through the shim;
  gated to suse_version >= 1699 because python-tree-sitter does not
  exist in Leap 16.0.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Jul 27 08:36:25 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package of tree-sitter-groovy 0.1.2:
  * Groovy grammar library for the tree-sitter parsing
    framework (libtree-sitter-groovy.so grammar module)
  * BuildRequires tree-sitter-java-devel: the grammar extends that
    grammar and tree-sitter generate resolves it from the devel
    package
  * Python binding built from the bundled bindings/python as
    pythonXYZ flavor subpackages via the shared
    %treesitter_python_build/_install macros
